What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_accel_self_test
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_anglvel_self_test
KernelVersion:	6.1
Contact:	fyy0619-cell <fyy0619-cell@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Read-only. Triggers the on-chip factory self-test actuators for
		the accelerometer or gyroscope, measures the self-test response
		(actuator enabled minus disabled) and reports the result as:

		    pass x=1 y=1 z=1

		"pass" is emitted only when all three axes fall inside the
		datasheet self-test-response window; otherwise "fail" is shown
		with the per-axis pass flags. Reading is only permitted while
		the buffer is disabled (direct mode).

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_accel_scale_available
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_anglvel_scale_available
KernelVersion:	6.1
Contact:	fyy0619-cell <fyy0619-cell@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Read-only. Space-separated list of supported scales (SI units
		per LSB) corresponding to the four hardware full-scale ranges
		(accel +/-2/4/8/16 g, gyro +/-250/500/1000/2000 dps). Writing
		one of these values to in_accel_scale / in_anglvel_scale
		selects the matching range.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/sampling_frequency_available
KernelVersion:	6.1
Contact:	fyy0619-cell <fyy0619-cell@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Read-only. Supported output data rates in Hz
		(10 25 50 100 200 500 1000), programmed through SMPLRT_DIV.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/buffer/hwfifo_watermark
KernelVersion:	6.1
Contact:	fyy0619-cell <fyy0619-cell@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Number of samples to batch in the on-chip 1 KiB FIFO before an
		interrupt drains them to the IIO buffer. A watermark of 0 or 1
		selects one-interrupt-per-sample data-ready mode; larger values
		reduce interrupt and wakeup load at the cost of latency.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/events/in_accel_mag_rising_en
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/events/in_accel_mag_rising_value
KernelVersion:	6.1
Contact:	fyy0619-cell <fyy0619-cell@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Motion-detection (wake-on-movement) event. Writing 1 to _en
		arms the accelerometer motion interrupt; _value sets the
		threshold in raw MOT_THR counts (LSB ~= 32 mg, range 0..255).
		A rising magnitude event is pushed to the event FIFO whenever
		acceleration exceeds the threshold.
